feat(docker): add Dockerfile and wire an api service into compose.yaml

Multi-stage Dockerfile (node:22.22.3-alpine, matching .nvmrc):
- deps: shared npm ci layer
- dev: hot-reload target (npm run dev), expects source bind-mounted
- build + prod-deps + prod: compiles via tsc, installs prod-only deps,
  runs the compiled dist/ with npm start

compose.yaml gets a new api service (defaults to the dev target so
`docker compose up` matches the existing local dev experience), depending
on mongodb's existing healthcheck. MONGO_CONN_STR is overridden via
environment: to the mongodb service's Docker-network hostname, since
.env's 127.0.0.1 value is only correct for a process running on the host.

Verified: docker compose build + up -d brings up both services; GET
/docs/openapi.json returns 200 and POST /auth/login with bad credentials
returns 401 (proving the containerized API reaches MongoDB through the
compose network, not just that the container is running).
